Fix: CSIdump forwarded nothing against the mt76 CSI driver built here.
Base: github.com/MtkWifiRev/MtkCSIdump @ 276b4b0814a283dcbc6544a76033e0e37154f092

CSIdump was written against a DIFFERENT mt76 vendor ABI than the 2022
MediaTek CSI patch we build. Two enumerators are missing from its copies of
the attribute enums, so every attribute number past them was off by one:
  CTRL: our driver has STA_INTERVAL between INTERVAL and DUMP_NUM
  DATA: our driver has DATA_NUM between TA and I, and ends CHAIN_INFO not H_IDX

Failure chain. CSIdump put DUMP_NUM at attr 8, which is the driver's
STA_INTERVAL (policy NLA_U32); a 2-byte u16 payload failed the driver's
nla_parse minimum-length check, so the dumpit returned -EINVAL and emitted
NOTHING. The ring therefore never drained (a unit sat pinned at 3000) and the
dump callback never ran. Even had the request landed, the driver replies with
DATA at attr 10 while CSIdump looked at attr 9, so the callback would have
returned NL_SKIP at its first check with no message printed. And the error
print used a stale ret that was always 0, so any failure read as 'Success'.
